  "_notes": [
    "bay: the card asks for three foam dummies to warm up the trigger on. No dummy is a placeable thing in the blockout format (only waves spawn Foamers, and a wave would lock the bay), so the three dummies are small voxel foam-white pieces at x -5.5, 0 and 6, z -7 to -9: they carve like any cover, go down in a few darts and cannot shoot back.",
    "explore-1: the S1 vent is [Paul] and not built; the foam-yellow marking at [5, -30] in the room's south-west corner marks its empty spot.",
    "pit: the pit floor is 4 m down and its south and west ledges are at bay level. The two ramps are 8 m and 6 m runs at about 27 and 34 degrees, both inside the nav grid's 40 degree slope, so a Swarmer can chase the player up and down them. The centre block (6 x 3.2 x 4 m in four 3.2 m zones) and the two pillars are voxel pieces; the block is a little lower than the concept's 3.5 m because a voxel zone may not exceed 3.2 m on any axis.",
    "yard: six islands, one 3.2 x 2.5 x 3.2 m voxel zone each (tops at -1.5 m, 2.5 m over the floor) with a 2.5 m ramp up the inner face. The ramp is inside the nav grid's 40 degree slope, and the nav test walks up and back down every one, so no Foamer is stranded. The east and west gates are sealed: the concept opens them in a later beat.",
    "breather: the U1 station is [Paul] and not built; the foam-yellow floor marking at [3, -71] marks its empty spot. No health pickup here, as the card says.",
    "waves: every wave is under 12 Swarmers alive (six, eight and ten), and the nearest Swarmer to the spawn cap is the Pit's second wave at eight.",
    "hall: the A4 lane runs north from the Yard's gate to a hole in its floor. Bare 6 m of lane is the drop, with 3 m floor ledges either side and an open hatch (drop-hatch) over it; the hatch starts open and the seal shuts it. Three of the six columns are voxel zones at the 3.2 m cap, three are 4 m shell columns, as the concept's split asks.",
    "hall chase: no lock and no door, 12 Swarmers from two rifts at the lane's mouth, one every 4 s, so the player can outrun them. The arena ends by the escape box on breather 2's floor, not by a clear: entering it asks the page to take the Foamers off the board (they cannot follow a 6 m drop) and seals drop-hatch 3 s after the landing. No unlockOnClear door, because nothing was cleared.",
    "breather2: the 10 x 8 m room sits 6 m under the hall, so the walk from the drop's foot through the Ring's south door is one floor. The U2 station and the S3 ledge are [Paul] and not built; the foam-yellow marking at [3.5, -152] and the lime marking at [-7, -150.5] mark their empty spots. The ammo is the concept's second A3 (section 6 lists A3 for both the Yard's west end and here), so it uses the new id breather2-ammo, 35 darts.",
    "ring: A2 30 x 30 m with the 10 x 8 x 3.5 m centre block as shell and four 1.6 x 1.6 x 2.8 m voxel pillars in the 6 m ring, one zone each. The block is 3.5 m, so its top is reached by a 1.5 m step on the east face, a 1.3 m step on top of that (both shell, 2 m deep), then a 0.7 m jump, all inside the player's 1.5 m mantle. The north door (ring-out) opens when the arena clears, alongside ring-in.",
    "ring waves: the concept's wave 2 is 12 Swarmers and 4 Roamers at once, which would put 16 Foamers alive, over the KIT cap of 12 and the validator's 16 error line. It is two waves instead: 12 Swarmers, then the 4 Roamers 2 s after they are down, so the Roamers still arrive last and shoot over a spent swarm.",
    "waves: every wave is under 12 Swarmers alive (six, eight, ten, twelve and twelve), and the nearest to the cap are the Pit's second wave and the Ring's second, at twelve.",
    "s3: the hall's 3 m floor ledges either side of the drop are also its S3 spot; the lime marking sits on the west one, 1.5 m over the room's floor below."
  ]
